From fb02fc4c4a0d069cd5c53ef80a242bfbee1567fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 16:43:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add the proactive interaction kernel and the DSH agent plugin

loop/core is a pure-Kotlin kernel for proactive interactions:

- Coordinator (T4): one active event, a small priority queue with merge
  and drop rules, and arbitration that only reads DSH's state through a
  Gate. It never shows anything while a phone task runs, a DSH question
  is open or a permission page is in front, and withdraws a page that is
  already up. Every agent attempt has its own requestId and every surface
  its own token, so late replies, old pages and expired buttons change
  nothing. Every change is persisted atomically; recovery resumes the
  agent poll with the same requestId and closes pages that died.
- ProactiveScheduler (T6): randomness only when planning; the decision
  is deterministic (quiet hours, daily cap counting deliveries, user
  activity, backoff after confirmed-ignored messages, pause, elapsed-time
  due checks so wall-clock changes cannot rush or delay an attempt,
  reboot and missed-slot handling, safe degradation without alarms).
- AgentWire (T8): decodes the plugin's answers into accepted / claimed /
  generated / failed without overstating any of them.

runtime/proactive/dsh-go-proactive is a zero-dependency DSH host plugin
that hands one event to a live, idle session as a followup turn and
tracks it through the session's own events. It never creates or wakes
sessions, refuses busy agents, sends at most once per requestId and per
eventId, and never hands out text that arrives after a cancel.

Tests: 66 JVM tests (kernel, scheduler, wire, the full chain, round 1),
10 plugin unit tests, and a 26-check live test against a real
@deepseek-ai/dsh 0.2.1-rc.4 engine with a local mock model.

